f Physical AI Skip to the content Skip to the Navigation About Technology Localization and Mapping Autonomous Navigation Spatial Intelligence and Analytics Robotics Robotics Solution Software Hardware Digital Twin Digital Twin Solution SW/HW XGRIDS SW/HW Vehicle MMS News IR Info. IR TOP IR NEWS IR Library Contact EN JP COMPANY Company Eyes for All Machines CEO Message Kudan pursues the vision of becoming “the eyes of every machine,” advancing spatial perception that leads the development of Physical AI. Our technologies provide the foundation for machines to understand, act, and learn within the real world—capabilities we believe are essential for Physical AI to permeate society and for robots and digital twins to operate in a highly integrated manner. Physical AI extends intelligence from the digital domain into the physical world, enabling machines to function safely and autonomously. At its core lies spatial perception: understanding the world in 3D, detecting continuous change, and determining optimal actions. By deeply focusing on this domain, Kudan is building the technological base that enables robotics and digital twins to become central components of future social systems. We view robotics and digital twins not simply as tools for efficiency but as transformative forces that will reshape industries and society. Robotics driven by spatial intelligence can address urgent societal needs such as labor shortages, safety improvements, and mobility in aging societies. Digital twins recreate the real world digitally, allowing industries to optimize productivity, strengthen resilience, and achieve sustainability. The real breakthrough emerges when robotics and digital twins are linked through spatial perception and evolve into true Physical AI. Robots act more intelligently by referencing digital twins, while digital twins continually update through real-time robot perception—forming a powerful cycle that drives automation, prediction, and innovation across society. While grounded in deep technology, our vision ultimately aims to deliver meaningful solutions: addressing societal challenges while unlocking new opportunities for innovation and growth. Kudan will continue to leverage deep tech, global networks, and strong foresight to build a future where spatial intelligence and perception form the foundation of daily life. Managing Director & CEO Daiu Ko Company Overview Born Global. Pioneering the Frontier of Technology. 2011 Established Kudan Limited in Bristol, United Kingdom, as a deep-tech company specializing in computer vision for augmented reality (AR). 2014 Established Kudan Inc. in Japan as the group’s global headquarters and holding company. 2016 Integrated expertise in computer vision and expanded into the development and provision of Artificial Perception / SLAM technologies. 2018 Listed on the Tokyo Stock Exchange Growth Market (formerly Mothers). 2020 Acquired and integrated Artisense, a SLAM technology company based in Munich, Germany (now operating as Kudan Germany). 2021 Established Kudan US to strengthen business expansion in the North American market. 2022 Began commercial deployment of SLAM technologies in collaboration with global customers and partners. 2025 Expanded technological domains to Spatial Intelligence and Perception, advancing applications in Robotics and Digital Twin fields OVERVIEW Company Overview COMPANY NAME Kudan Inc. ESTABLISHED November 19, 2014 MARKET Tokyo Stock Exchange Growth Market Security Code: 4425 HEADQUARTERS 1-23-14 Jinnan, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0041, Japan BUSINESS R&D of Spatial Perception Technologies and the provision of software for Physical AI Group companies Kudan Limited Bristol, England Kudan USA LLC California, USA Kudan Vision Inc. Tokyo, Japan Kudan Germany Munich, Germany LEADERSHIP Board Member Managing Director & CEO Daiu Ko Mr. Ko graduated from the Faculty of Engineering, the University of Tokyo in 2007 and earned his Master’s Degree in Mechanical Engineering from the Graduate School of Engineering, the University of Tokyo in 2009. He began his career at Toyota Motor Corporation in 2009 and joined McKinsey & Company’s Tokyo Office in 2014. Mr. Ko joined Kudan Inc. in 2016 and was appointed Director and Chief Operating Officer (COO) in 2017. Since 2020, he has served as CEO of Artisense Corporation and Representative Director and Chief Executive Officer (CEO) of Kudan Inc. Managing Director Tomo Ohno Mr. Ohno graduated from the Faculty of Business Administration, Yokohama National University in 1993. He began his career at Andersen Consulting Tokyo (currently Accenture Japan Ltd.) and later transferred to Andersen Consulting UK (currently Accenture UK). He joined SN Systems Limited (UK) in 2002 and was appointed President of SN Systems Co., Ltd. in 2005. In the same year, he established Zen United Limited (UK), serving as Director. Mr. Ohno founded Kudan Limited in 2011 and has served as Representative Director since its inception. He also founded Kudan Inc. in 2014 and continues to serve as its Representative Director (current). Director & COO Tian Hao Mr. Hao graduated from the Faculty of Engineering, Hokkaido University in 2008 and earned his Master’s Degree in Electronic Information Engineering from the Graduate School of Information Science and Technology, the University of Tokyo in 2010. He began his professional career at Ericsson Japan K.K. (formerly Nippon Ericsson K.K.) in 2010. Mr. Hao joined Kudan Inc. in 2021, was appointed Executive Officer and Chief Revenue Officer (CRO) in 2022, and has served as Director and Chief Operating Officer (COO) since 2023. Director Reiko Asano Ms. Asano began her career at NTT DOCOMO, INC. in 2005. She joined Kudan Inc. in 2024 and was appointed CEO, Japan Region in 2025, where she leads the company's domestic business operations and drives growth in the Japanese market. She has served as Director since 2026 (current). External Director, Audit & Supervisory Committee Member Shinichi Misawa Mr. Misawa began his career at Daiwa Securities Co. Ltd. in 1989. He was appointed President and Representative Director of D-Brain Securities Co., Ltd. in 1997 and later joined transcosmos inc. in 1999, where he served as Senior Executive Managing Director and CFO from 2004. In 2006, he founded Co-Creation Partners Co., Ltd., where he continues to serve as Representative Director. Mr. Misawa has also held several external board and auditor positions, including Outside Corporate Auditor of Frontier International Inc. (current) and Outside Director and Audit and Supervisory Committee Member of JIG-SAW Inc. (current). He was appointed Outside Director of Kudan Inc. in 2015 and continues to serve as Outside Director and Audit and Supervisory Committee Member (current). External Director, Audit & Supervisory Committee Member Hisanori Oguri Mr. Oguri began his career at Toshiba Corporation in 1992. He joined Takeda Minoru Law Office in 2001 and later Jones Day Tokyo in 2010. In 2012, he joined Uchida & Samejima Law Firm (currently Uchida & Samejima Law Office) and became a Partner in 2014, a position he continues to hold. Mr. Oguri was appointed Outside Corporate Auditor of Kudan Inc. in 2017 and currently serves as Outside Director and Audit and Supervisory Committee Member. He also serves as Director and Audit and Supervisory Committee Member of Howe Television, Inc. (current). External Director, Audit & Supervisory Committee Member Takashi Miida Mr. Miida began his career at Deloitte Touche Tohmatsu LLC in 2008. He established Miida Certified Public Accountant Office in 2013, where he continues to serve as Representative. In 2014, he founded WORLD TROTTER Co., Ltd. and has served as Representative Director since its establishment. Mr. Miida was appointed Outside Director and Audit and Supervisory Committee Member of Kudan Inc. in 2024 (current). Follow Us X YouTube LinkedIn JP EN Follow Us X YouTube LinkedIn JP EN About Technology Localization and Mapping Autonomous Navigation Spatial Intelligence and Analytics Robotics Solution Software Hardware Digital Twin Solution SW/HW XGRIDS SW/HW Vehicle MMS News IR Info. IR NEWS IR Library Contact Copyright © Kudan Inc.｜Spatial Perception Technology Driving the Advancement of Physical AI All Rights Reserved. MENU About Technology Localization and Mapping Autonomous Navigation Spatial Intelligence and Analytics Robotics Robotics Solution Software Hardware Digital Twin Digital Twin Solution SW/HW XGRIDS SW/HW Vehicle MMS News IR Info. IR TOP IR NEWS IR Library Contact EN JP This website uses cookies to improve your experience. We'll assume you're ok with this, but you can opt-out if you wish. Cookie settings ACCEPT Privacy & Cookies Policy Close Privacy Overview This website uses cookies to improve your experience while you navigate through the website. Out of these cookies, the cookies that are categorized as necessary are stored on your browser as they are essential for the working of basic functionalities of the website. We also use third-party cookies that help us analyze and understand how you use this website. These cookies will be stored in your browser only with your consent. You also have the option to opt-out of these cookies. But opting out of some of these cookies may have an effect on your browsing experience. Necessary Necessary Always Enabled Necessary cookies are absolutely essential for the website to function properly. This category only includes cookies that ensures basic functionalities and security features of the website. These cookies do not store any personal information. Non-necessary Non-necessary Any cookies that may not be particularly necessary for the website to function and is used specifically to collect user personal data via analytics, ads, other embedded contents are termed as non-necessary cookies. It is mandatory to procure user consent prior to running these cookies on your website. SAVE & ACCEPT Back to top"
